  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x563">
    <title>CHT Hardware Present</title>
    <description>Defines if a Cylinder Head Temp Sensor is Fitted. Not set means the sensor is an ECT sensor.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Most scan tools expect the EEC to report temperature of the cylinder head, in which case those scan tools will no longer function if this is disabled (As they will report the dead CHT value)</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="77" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x124B4" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x4B6">
    <title>VCT Hardware Present</title>
    <description>Defines if VCT is fitted to the vehicle. Set = VCT is fitted</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="9" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1208A" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x5414">
    <title>VCT Hardware Inverse</title>
    <description>Defines if VCT signal is inverse. Set means that the VCT is the inverse of the factory configuration (Computer Commanding Advance = Cam Retards).</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="9" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1208B" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x2E3F">
    <title>OBD Compliance Mode</title>
    <description>Sc0878 - Labled as j1979_01_1c. J1979 is the OBD standard that defines basiclly every essential code. The next 4 charactors seem to be the hex commands relating to how an OBD adaptor checks what the vehicle supports. The value stored at this location seems to be the supported OBD mode, shown here as decimal. The recommended range from the ford symbol table is 1-5, which would line up with the below support codes:&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;OBD compliance:&#013;&#010;0x01 = OBD II (California ARB)&#013;&#010;0x02 = OBD (US Federal EPA)&#013;&#010;0x03 = OBD and OBD II&#013;&#010;0x04 = OBD I&#013;&#010;0x05 = Not OBD compliant&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;The factory value seems to be &quot;Not OBD compliant&quot;. Although not recommended, changing this value might allow some OBD tools to connect to the car, as the protocol for communicating with the EEC-V from the AU is actually supported by OBD-II.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="78" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x12062" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>Mode</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <rangehigh>0.000000</rangehigh>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x5720">
    <title>Allow Tip-In Knock Reduction</title>
    <description>Controls a strange knock intergration. Enabled means Tip-in only triggers when a Knock event is detected.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Enabled thus gives slightly better Tip-In response.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="43" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x12E02" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x5F81">
    <title>Allow Tip-In Closed Loop Spark Logic</title>
    <description>Allow Tip-In Spark Logic to Run during Closed Loop Fueling. Disabled Means PT or WOT only.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="43" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x12E01" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0xE23">
    <title>Allow Tip-In Spark Logic</title>
    <description>Allow any Tip-In spark logic to run. Disabled = No Tip-In Spark Control.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="43" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x12E00" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
