  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x1869" vislevel="1" flags="0x0">
    <title>ACT - Retard per Degree C Multiplier</title>
    <description>This table controls a multiplier that is applied to the preposed spark retard for ACT.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Normally, without this table the system behaves as follows:&#013;&#010;ACT Retard from BDLN = ACT - ACT Threshold. Where Every Degree of ACT over the threshold is 0.25 Degrees of spark retard.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This table multiplies the resulting ACT value based on RPM and MAP to reduce the effect of the spark retard in some areas.</description>
