  <XDFFUNCTION uniqueid="0x4AE9" flags="0x0">
    <title>ACT Threshold to begin BDLN Retard</title>
    <description>This function controls the threshold ACT temperature, after which ACT retard begins. Think of this as the midway point for ACT. If ACT gets lower than this than timing is added to Borderline. If ACT gets higher than this, timing is taken away.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Input is EGR Flow&#013;&#010;Output is ACT Threshold to begin spark retard from BDLN</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="44" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x127A6" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedcolcount="7" mmedmajorstridebits="16" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>EGR Flow</units>
      <indexcount>7</indexcount>
      <embedinfo type="1" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X/4">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x01" mmedaddress="0x127A7" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedcolcount="7" mmedmajorstridebits="16" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>ACT Thresh</units>
      <indexcount>7</indexcount>
      <embedinfo type="1" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
  </XDFFUNCTION>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x78CB">
    <title>Upper Limit for Spk Retard ACT</title>
    <description>This provides a high clip for the ACT spark retard value. Preventing its value from becoming too high (Taking away too much timing).&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Think of this as the maximum amount of timing the ACT Correction will be able to remove.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="44" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x01" mmedaddress="0x126E2" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>*C</units>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x933">
    <title>Estimated Maximum ACT Retard</title>
    <description>This scaler is designed to show the maximum ACT retard from Borderline that will be possible. Assuming the Multiplier table is filled with 0.5. It isn&apos;t recommended to use this scaler to configure the system.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="44" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x01" mmedaddress="0x126E2" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>Degrees</units>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="0.125*X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x2523">
    <title>Lower Limit for Spk Retard ACT</title>
    <description>This provides a low clip for the ACT spark retard value. Preventing its value from becoming too low (Adding too much positive timing).&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This is important because the ACT Borderline Correction can actually ADD timing to Borderline, which can be dangerous if too much timing is eventually added.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Think of this as the maximum amount of timing the ACT Correction will be able to add.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="44" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x01" mmedaddress="0x126E3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>*C</units>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x723D">
    <title>Estimated Maximum ACT Advance</title>
    <description>This scaler is designed to show the maximum ACT retard from Borderline that will be possible. Assuming the Multiplier table is filled with 0.5. It isn&apos;t recommended to use this scaler to configure the system.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Note even though a Negative value is shown. The Spark will be advanced, not retarded.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="4" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="41" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="44" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x01" mmedaddress="0x126E3" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>Degrees</units>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="0.125*X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
