  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x7BA0" flags="0x0">
    <title>OL Fuel Target - Temperature over Load Term</title>
    <description>Open Loop Fuel Target - Temperature over Load Term&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This is the LAMSE target dependent on ECT to ACT Delta (Effective Engine Temperature) and Load. If the Lamda values in this table are lower than the Lambda values in the N over Load Term Table, then these values will be used, otherwise the N over Load Term Table values are used.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;When you setup your fueling, you should use this table to control the desired LAMSE until the engine has warmed up to your desired ECT over ACT, then once the engine is warm, fill all the columms that are higher than your desired temperature with 1.0 lambda (or 14.64 AFR target) so the Fueling Calculation switches over to the N over Load Term Table.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="50" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="59" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>deg C</units>
      <indexcount>10</indexcount>
      <embedinfo type="2" linkobjid="0x703B" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>MAP/BP</units>
      <indexcount>9</indexcount>
      <embedinfo type="2" linkobjid="0xEFA" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
