  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x6E23" vislevel="1" flags="0x0">
    <title>HEGO Bias / GSM Fraction LPG</title>
    <description>Hego Bias defines how Rich or Lean closed loop will tend to run the car. This is an odd mechanism of the EEC computer, which effectivly allowed it to push closed loop AFRs slightly outside the normal range of a narrowband sensor.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;When setup correctly with a well tuned O2 sensor, it can affectivly allow you to run the car slightly richer or slightly leaner that stoich at a given RPM and load.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Negative Values provide a more rich running closed loop.&#013;&#010;Positive Values provide a more lean running closed loop.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="56" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="62" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
