  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x352E" flags="0x0">
    <title>Shift Pressure Ramp Phase 1 - Pressure at 0% Torque</title>
    <description>Defines the targeted S5 current when the transmission torque final input is 0% effective engine torque (From engine torque tables). This is used to decide line pressure by forming a slope when the transmission is in phase 1 of any shift. Phase 1&apos;s pressure is based on taking the basic non shifting pressure and applying an offset to it, phase 2 then applies yet another offset.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Higher values might encourage a faster shift and reduce slip in the shift, but cause a more harsh feeling shift.</description>
