  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x291B" flags="0x0">
    <title>Shift Pressure Ramp Phase 2 - Additive Pressure at 0% Torque</title>
    <description>Defines the additional change in S5 current when the transmission torque final input is 0% effective engine torque (From engine torque tables). This is used to decide line pressure by increasing the initial command from phase 1 by a given amount as the transmission moves into phase 2 of a shift. This is usually the longest stage of the shift, as phase 1 moves line pressure to the point where RPM begins to drag down / up, and phase 2 actually moves the transmission between the gears.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Higher values might encourage a faster shift and reduce slip in the shift, but cause a more harsh feeling shift.</description>
