  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x1863">
    <title>Standby / Conclusion S5 Current</title>
    <description>Current delivered to S5 when it is not activly being commanded to control the pressure in a shift. Lower mA might allow the BTR to hold more power when not shifting.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This current gets applied after shift phase 2, while waiting for the Finish Delay to expire and return the transmission to base pressure.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="20" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="28" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x15DA8" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>mA</units>
    <rangehigh>0.000000</rangehigh>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x17A8" flags="0x0">
    <title>S6 Valve Pressure Bump Control - Activation Delay</title>
    <description>Defines the time to wait before &quot;bumping&quot; the S6 solinoid, which is used to further kick line pressure up during a shift in condtions where even more shift pressure is required, as defined by external thresholds.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Lower values make S6 pressure introduction start sooner, which could firm up shifts when S5 has already been tuned to its limit.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="20" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="29" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <indexcount>43</indexcount>
