  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x3F28" flags="0x0">
    <title>S6 Valve Pressure Bump Control - Minimum Activation Duration</title>
    <description>Defines the minimum time that after the activation delay, the S6 valve is &quot;Bumped&quot;, which is used to further kick line pressure up during a shift in condtions where even more shift pressure is required, as defined by external thresholds.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Values decide effectively the minimum S6 kicking time, higher values can help &quot;lock&quot; s6 on during a shift providing substantially more shifting force but might cause S6 to stay on longer than the shift actually takes.</description>
