  <XDFTABLE uniqueid="0x5C49" flags="0x0">
    <title>S6 Valve Pressure Bump Control - Basic Activation Duration</title>
    <description>Defines the basic time that after the activation delay, the S6 valve is &quot;Bumped&quot;, which is used to further kick line pressure up during a shift in condtions where even more shift pressure is required, as defined by external thresholds.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Values decide effectively the enforced S6 kicking time, higher values can help &quot;lock&quot; s6 on during a shift providing substantially more shifting force in cases where the shift takes longer to complete / on more worn transmissions. But usually, S6 just follows the shift progress as indicated by the state of S5.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="7" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="20" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="29" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
