    <title>Shift Classification Matrix - Low Load Low Speed</title>
    <description>Defines the Shift Class (Used downstream to pick slope terms for converting torque to S5 signal) depending on the current gear and next gear. This table gets used in special lower load / speed condtions and normally commands for less &quot;harsh&quot; shift profiles, from stock altering all single gear downshifts.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Considering this controls everything down to the solinoid actuations applied for the gear change, editing is discouraged.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Columns: Desired Gear&#013;&#010;Rows: Current (Actually) Selected Gear</description>
