    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X/2">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x67B3">
    <title>Fuel Total Drive Sum Enable</title>
    <description>Defines if the rolling fuel sum calculation is enabled.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;There are two active calculations. The Fuel lph calculation is used to calculate L/100km on the ECU and then send it to the dashboard via DOL. The Fuel Sum calculation however records the total fuel consumed since EEC power up, its not known what it is used for, it may be sent over DOL as well.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This switch enables or disables the Total Sum calculation, the L/100km calculation will not be affected.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="79" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="86" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x1351F" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x1921">
    <title>DOL Fuel Consumption Scaling Factor</title>
    <description>Defines the scaling factor that turns actual L/100km into the raw value sent over DOL for the dashboard. Can be used to inflate or under-report fuel consumption to DOL.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="79" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="86" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x126BC" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>Factor</units>
    <decimalpl>7</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X/8388608">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFFUNCTION uniqueid="0x5955" flags="0x0">
    <title>Injector Dead Time - Battery Voltage</title>
    <description>Injector Dead Time is a measure of how long the Injector takes to open when it is powered. The EEC-V rather than storing this as a single value, maps it against battery voltage to compensate for differing charge states.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Edit when changing injectors. Values for this function should be available from your injector Manufacturer. Injector Manufacturers may also only provide a dead time for a single voltage, in which cause just use the same MS dead time for all the Y values.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="6" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="79" />
    <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x136C0" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedcolcount="9" mmedmajorstridebits="-16" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>vBat</units>
      <indexcount>9</indexcount>
      <max>0.000000</max>
      <embedinfo type="1" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X/16">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
    <XDFAXIS id="y" uniqueid="0x0">
      <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x136C1" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedcolcount="9" mmedmajorstridebits="-16" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
      <units>Dead Time - ms</units>
      <indexcount>9</indexcount>
      <max>0.000000</max>
      <embedinfo type="1" />
      <datatype>0</datatype>
      <unittype>0</unittype>
      <DALINK index="0" />
      <MATH equation="X/32">
        <VAR id="X" />
      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
  </XDFFUNCTION>
