      </MATH>
    </XDFAXIS>
  </XDFFUNCTION>
  <XDFFUNCTION uniqueid="0x7BED" flags="0x0">
    <title>Idle Speed Deviation vs Corrective Spark (Open Loop Idle)</title>
    <description>Corrects the Base Idle Spark Advance relative to the amount of error between the current RPM and Desired RPM. RPM is shown in the left columm as required change to reach Desired Engine Speed.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Example, 400 RPM higher than desired is shown as -400, as the Engine RPM needs to be reduced by 400 to reach the desired RPM.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;For bogans looking to make there Intech sound lumpy, make the spark correction values on the right very aggressive. Your welcome ;)</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="3" />
