  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xCC8">
    <title>EEC Clock Speed Flag?</title>
    <description>Careful! - This value could not be correctly matched to N9XJ4 (Contains previously thought impossable value)&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This is the EEC&apos;s clockspeed flag, which tells the EEC how convert various values and keep track of time. There are 5 acceptable inputs here:&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;4 = 27 Mhz Clockspeed&#013;&#010;3 = 23 Mhz Clockspeed&#013;&#010;2 = 21 Mhz Clockspeed&#013;&#010;1 = 18 Mhz Clockspeed&#013;&#010;0 = 15 Mhz Clockspeed&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;It is highly discouraged to edit this value, rather it is intended as an indicator for advanced users on what the Corrections for various values are going to be.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;</description>
