  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x31C0">
    <title>Invert EGO Input</title>
    <description>Defines if the input pin for the o2 sensor should be inverted or not. When using the advanced HEGO patch with a techedge, you need to turn this off.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Set = Pin is Inverted (1.6v internally is 0v, visa versa)&#013;&#010;Not Set = Raw Input is used directly&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Factory is set here, due to the design of the stock sensor.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="53" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x13566" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x42DC">
    <title>EGO Allow Failure Monitoring</title>
    <description>Defines if the HEGO self testing processes are allowed to run. Not set will inhibit all HEGO testing and the HEGO will always be declared fault free and operational.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Set means the HEGO will be checked and can be declared failed.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="53" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x17EE7" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFFLAG uniqueid="0x416B">
    <title>Stablise Idle before allowing Idle C/L</title>
    <description>Defines if the Idle effectivly needs to be stable before C/L is allowed at Idle or if C/L will always be allowed during idle.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Clear for the adaptive idle fuel cells to used as soon as the filtered airmass region is entered. Set for the adaptive idle fuel cells to used only when in the filtered airmass region and there are no base idle rpm adders being applied.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="2" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="64" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x14212" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
