  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x1EB1">
    <title>RPM Error from Desired to start CL Idle</title>
    <description>Deviation from the Desired RPM of the EEC to start Closed Loop Idle control.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;During the EECs Idle Control Routine, when the target RPM is reached at a defined stability, closed loop idle (PID) is disabled and the last ISC Duty Cycle value is held by open loop mode. However, if the engine RPM changes from the desired RPM by the value in this scaler, Closed Loop Idle will be re-enabled to find the required ISC duty cycle again.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="3" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="31" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedtypeflags="0x02" mmedaddress="0x149B6" mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>RPM Error</units>
    <rangehigh>0.000000</rangehigh>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X/4">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x27BD">
    <title>RPM Error from Desired to start CL Hysterisis</title>
    <description>Sc0315 - This value is used as a hysterisis that forms an upper limit of how much RPM deviation is allowed in closed loop, before open loop should take back over and fix closed loops idle error.</description>
