    <mask>0x01</mask>
  </XDFFLAG>
  <XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x7AD9">
    <title>Patch Normalised Load Calculation for Boost</title>
    <description>Replaces a SHRDW instruction in the normalised load calculation with a SHLDW instruction. Which changes a divisor applied to map before normal load is calculated into a multiplier.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This allows normal load to interpret map correctly and reach values of up to 2.0</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="12" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Replace Instrucion" address="0x25C13" datasize="0x1" patchdata="0D" basedata="0C" />
  </XDFPATCH>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x200B">
    <title>OBDII - Bits to shift left during MAP conversion to OBD MAP (PIDMAP)</title>
    <description>Boost Compatilibity Byte. Use this to change the multiplier applied to MAP by the shlw instruction when MAP is being converted from a byte to a word for reading by a diagnostic tool.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Set this value to 2 instead of 1 to correct the MAP reading shown by diagnostic tools when using a boost ready binary. Otherwise in diagnostic tools the reading of map will be half the true reading, eg: 50kpa in OBD reader = 100 actual kpa.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="12" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x24C7" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>Shift Bit Count</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0xB1">
    <title>VE - Bits to shift left during VE Computation</title>
    <description>Number of bits to shift over during the calculation of VE. Use this to greatly increase fueling AS A LAST RESORT.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;It is highly recommended to use BASEMD (Displacement), KVEFF (Engine Airmass Multiplier) or the Injector Slope to increase fuel delivery first, before attempting to edit this value.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Usage example:&#013;&#010;Increasing this by 1 and deviding the VE table by 2 will result in the same final VE / fuel required being calculated.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="12" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x25A44" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>Shift Bit Count</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x65DC">
    <title>VE - Bits to shift left during Normal Load Computation</title>
    <description>Number of bits to shift MAP over by before MAP is used in the normalised load calculaton.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Use this to greatly affect the results of the normalised load calculation.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Note that for the bits to shift left, the &quot;Patch Normalised Load Calculation for Boost&quot; patch must be applied, otherwise this will control how many bits to shift right, rather than left, which will behave like a MAP divider rather than a multiplier.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="12" />
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedaddress="0x25C14" mmedelementsizebits="8" mmedmajorstridebits="0" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
    <units>Shift Bit Count</units>
    <decimalpl>0</decimalpl>
    <datatype>0</datatype>
    <unittype>0</unittype>
    <DALINK index="0" />
    <MATH equation="X">
      <VAR id="X" />
    </MATH>
  </XDFCONSTANT>
  <XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x50BB">
    <title>Legacy - Disable and Block Non Open Loop writes to LAMBSE</title>
    <description>Legacy Patch - Not recommended for use.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Due to great complexities with how LAMBSE is shared between the open loop fueling code and closed loop fueling code. Even when the O2 sensor logic is disabled via flag, misbehavour with LAMBSE can still occur.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This glitch is normally observed at idle when closed loop fueling is disabled, and open loop fueling is commanding 1.0. LAMBSE can be seen frequently cycling between 14.64 AFR and approximetly 13.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;This patch takes a crude approch to the problem, and will overwrite any attempts to set the value of LAMBSE with FF, unless the attempts are coming from the known open loop fuel function which sets LAMBSE to the values calculated from the Main Fueling Tables.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;NOTE, This WILL very likely break the following features:&#013;&#010;-Closed Loop Fueling&#013;&#010;-Mininum and Maximum LAMBSE clips&#013;&#010;-Torque Management via Fuel&#013;&#010;-MPG mode&#013;&#010;-LPG operation</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="19" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 8D849 Block" address="0x2E014" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628634" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 873F9 Block" address="0x27410" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628644" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 86840 Block" address="0x26975" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362864A" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 8667B-3 Block" address="0x26744" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628626" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 8667B-2 Block" address="0x2672F" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628626" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 8667B Block" address="0x2671F" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628626" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 860F2 Block" address="0x26105" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362863E" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 85F45-2 Block" address="0x260A3" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362863C" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 85F45 Block" address="0x2603B" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362863C" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 85F35 Block" address="0x25F40" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362864A" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 85C40 Block" address="0x25EAF" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362864A" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 52C0 Block" address="0x52D6" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362864A" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 4B13-4 Block" address="0x4B76" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628634" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 4B13-3 Block" address="0x4B64" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628634" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 4B13-2 Block" address="0x4B57" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628634" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 4B13 Block" address="0x4B45" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628634" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 4AEA Block" address="0x4AEF" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C3628634" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Sub 48F4 Block" address="0x490D" datasize="0x4" patchdata="FFFFFFFF" basedata="C362864A" />
  </XDFPATCH>
  <XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x33A2">
    <title>Legacy - IMRC Hard Cut Spark Mod (Beta)</title>
    <description>Old Patch, removal recommended.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Configures the tail end of the IMRC code to trigger a spark cut when the IMRC Minimum RPM is reached. Maximum RPM should be set to 16384.75&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Use the Minimum RPM Hysterisis to control the RPM drop.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="19" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="use IMRC to set the bits two" address="0x2C2A6" datasize="0x3" patchdata="717FEF" basedata="71DFAD" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="use IMRC to set the bits firs" address="0x2C2A1" datasize="0x3" patchdata="9180EF" basedata="9120AD" />
  </XDFPATCH>
  <XDFPATCH uniqueid="0x4889">
    <title>WOT Timing Soft Spark Cut Mod</title>
    <description>Allows using the Spark Adder for WOT function to reduce timing instead of adding timing at a given RPM under all condtions. This allows setting it up as a spark limiter.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="16" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Disable WOT Check" address="0x27066" datasize="0x3" patchdata="FFFFFF" basedata="37790A" />
  </XDFPATCH>
  <XDFPATCH uniqueid="0xEDB">
    <title>Generation 3 Hard Spark Cutoff</title>
    <description>3rd Generation Hard Spark Cut Patch.&#013;&#010;&#013;&#010;Existing RPM Limit values are used, but spark is cut rather than fuel via command to the EDIS processor to drop coil signal.</description>
    <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="1" category="81" />
    <CATEGORYMEM index="2" category="16" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Flag Tamper Block B (LPG)" address="0x22ABD" datasize="0x3" patchdata="FFFFFF" basedata="717FEF" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Flag Tamper Block A (LPG)" address="0x22AAE" datasize="0x3" patchdata="FFFFFF" basedata="9180EF" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Cutoff Clear" address="0x26930" datasize="0x3" patchdata="717FEF" basedata="71FB7C" />
    <XDFPATCHENTRY name="Cutoff Set" address="0x26921" datasize="0x3" patchdata="9180EF" basedata="91047C" />
  </XDFPATCH>
